# Cursor Rule Template (AKOS integration)

Written to a project's `.cursor/rules/akos.mdc` by `akos install-project`. Cursor reads `.mdc` rule files with frontmatter.

```mdc
---
description: AKOS knowledge system integration
alwaysApply: true
---

# AKOS

This project uses AKOS (global knowledge system at ~/DEV/AKOS). For user-facing features, architecture, security, or data work, load the relevant AKOS knowledge before acting.

Bootstrap (read in order):
- ~/DEV/AKOS/core/constitution.md
- ~/DEV/AKOS/core/authority-model.md
- ~/DEV/AKOS/core/reasoning-profiles.md (profile in .akos/config.md)
- ~/DEV/AKOS/core/review-pipeline.md
- ~/DEV/AKOS/packs/personal/<personal_profile>/ (Level-0, always applies; <personal_profile> from this project's .akos/config.md, default pau-avila)

Then load the 2-5 task-relevant packs from ~/DEV/AKOS/packs/. For reviews use ~/DEV/AKOS/agents/ and the unified Review Summary format.

Safety floor (never waived, any profile): security, accessibility basics, data integrity.
Defaults: empty/loading/error/success states on every async surface; mobile-responsive by default; Supabase RLS at table creation for deployed projects; challenge unnecessary complexity; anti-template UI; direct actionable output.
```
